          ],
          "orig": "When a model that can Fly starts or ends a Charge move on a terrain feature, instead of measuring the path it has moved across the battlefield, you instead measure its path 'through the air'. In addition, it can be moved over other models as if they were not there. A model that can Fly cannot end any move on top of another model.",
          "text": "When a model that can Fly starts or ends a Charge move on a terrain feature, instead of measuring the path it has moved across the battlefield, you instead measure its path 'through the air'. In addition, it can be moved over other models as if they were not there. A model that can Fly cannot end any move on top of another model."
        }
